  "scope": "Normative registry for first-class/runtime interoperability concepts. Exhaustive v1 legacy leaf coverage is governed by V1_FIELD_MIGRATION.json; a migration target is a canonical semantic path but need not be promoted to a first-class registry concept.",
  "promotion_rule": "Add a first-class registry concept when it is exchanged across consumers, independently queried/reasoned over, or requires stable aliases/kind/cardinality metadata.",
  "storage_contract": "canonical_path is the semantic home. Relation/event instances are physically stored once in PersonaKernel.relations/events with stable IDs + canonical_path; the corresponding domain payload must not copy the same fact.",
  "contract_version": "2.0.0-rc2",
  "value_contract_policy": "Every first-class concept declares a storage mode and machine-oriented value contract. Consumer-specific schemas may refine but must not contradict these contracts.",
  "kind_policy": "Kinds apply to the semantic concept, not the namespace. A summary/profile may be a state even when its underlying observations concern processes or relations."
}
